On 28-10-14 12:39, Frank, Alvaro Jesus wrote:
> Wait, this creates binaries?

no, it creates a tar.gz file with the source files. Automake looks for
the variables that end in _SOURCES, _DIST, _DATA and a few others to
determine what needs to be added to the tar.gz file.
That's why a 'make distcheck' run shouldn't fail. It may indicate you
didn't add all required files to Makefile.am (and thus not to the tar.gz
file).


Lennart.

